---
// /privacy-policy — the site's only legal page.
//
// Built 2026-09-06 (Ollie). The homepage contact form has posted personal data
// to HubSpot since the June 2026 launch with no privacy policy anywhere on the
// site, and the old CosmOS site's /privacy-policy had been 404ing since the
// redesign (Search Console: "Crawled - currently not indexed", last crawled
// 23 Mar 2026). Reusing the old path rather than /privacy so the URL Google
// already knows resolves again.
//
// Brief was "as minimal as legally and physically possible". That is workable
// here only because the site genuinely collects almost nothing: no cookies, no
// analytics, no tag manager, no advertising or tracking pixels, and no HubSpot
// tracking script (the form posts straight to the Forms API instead). No cookie
// banner is needed while that stays true.
//
// EVERY CLAIM BELOW WAS VERIFIED AGAINST THE SOURCE ON 2026-09-06. If any of
// these change, this page has to change with them:
//   - public/index.html form -> api-eu1.hsforms.com (portal 143819223, EU1)
//   - the same form -> api.ipify.org for the visitor IP, on submit only
//   - Netlify hosting, so Netlify holds the server logs
//
// Fonts were the fourth entry here until 2026-09-06. They are now self-hosted
// from public/fonts/, so simply loading a page contacts nobody but Netlify.
// Putting a Google Fonts <link> back into any page means putting Google back
// into the list below.
// Adding any analytics or tracking to this site means rewriting section 2 and
// almost certainly adding a consent banner.
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';

const updated = '6 September 2026';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy policy — Sonical"
  description="What Sonical.ai collects, which is almost nothing. No cookies, no analytics, no tracking. The only personal data we hold is what you type into the contact form."
  canonical="https://www.sonical.ai/privacy-policy/"
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  heading='Privacy <span class="acc">policy</span>'
  nav=""
  centered={true}
>
  <p class="lede">
    This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics and does not track you. The only
    personal data we hold is what you type into the contact form. Everything
    below is the detail behind those two sentences.
  </p>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Sonical Inc, San Mateo, California. We are the data controller for this
      site. For anything on this page, write to
      <a href="mailto:info@sonical.ai">info@sonical.ai</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p><b>If you submit the contact form,</b> we receive:</p>
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li>Your name and email address</li>
      <li>The reasons for interest you tick</li>
      <li>Your IP address and the page you submitted from</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <b>When any page loads,</b> our host records a standard web server log entry:
      the request, your IP address and your browser's user agent.
    </p>
    <p>
      <b>That is everything.</b> No cookies, no analytics, no advertising or
      tracking pixels, no profiling, and nothing stored on your device. The
      fonts and images are served from our own domain rather than someone
      else's, so reading a page introduces you to nobody. Browse as much as you
      like and we learn nothing about you beyond a line in a server log.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Why we hold it</h2>
    <p>
      To reply to you, and to carry on the conversation if there is one worth
      having. We do not sell it, rent it or pass it to anyone for their own
      marketing. Under UK and EU data protection law our lawful basis is
      legitimate interest, specifically responding to an enquiry you chose to
      send us. Server logs exist to keep the site running and secure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Who else touches it</h2>
    <div class="rows">
      <div class="rowcard">
        <h3>HubSpot</h3>
        <p>
          Our CRM. Contact form submissions are stored here, in HubSpot's EU data
          centre.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rowcard">
        <h3>Netlify</h3>
        <p>Hosts the site and holds the server logs, on their retention schedule.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rowcard">
        <h3>ipify</h3>
        <p>
          When you submit the form, your browser asks ipify for your public IP so
          the enquiry is not blind to where it came from. On submit only.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Sonical is US-based, so an enquiry you send us is handled in the United
      States. Each of the services above is used for the single job described and
      none of them get your details for their own marketing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Enquiries stay in HubSpot until you ask us to delete them, or until they
      are plainly stale and we clear them out. Server logs are held by Netlify on
      their own schedule and we do not copy them anywhere.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:info@sonical.ai">info@sonical.ai</a> and we will act
      on it. You can ask us to show you what we hold, correct it, delete it, send
      you a copy, or stop contacting you. No form, no account, no hoops.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are in the UK or the EU you also have the right to complain to your
      national data protection authority. If you are in California, you have the
      right to know what we hold and to have it deleted. We do not sell personal
      information, and we never have.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we start collecting anything beyond what is described here, this page
      changes first. Last updated {updated}.
    </p>
    <div class="ctarow">
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/">Back to the homepage &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
